{
 "esm": "1.0.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "ScmPhysicsColumn",
  "description": "Single-column PHYSICS-DRIVER SUITE of the EqWeather reference case (WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy: mp_physics = 6 WSM6, ra_lw_physics = 1 RRTM, ra_sw_physics = 1 Dudhia, sf_sfclay_physics = 1 revised MM5, sf_surface_physics = 1 five-layer slab, bl_pbl_physics = 1 YSU, cu = shcu = fdda = 0), i.e. what WRF's radiation_driver, surface_driver and pbl_driver together do to one column in one time step. Eight components are mounted by reference as top-level systems and coupled in the WRF call order with variable_map/param_to_var edges (esm-spec 10.4): the RRTM longwave chain (RRTMColumn -> RRTMSetcoef -> RRTMGasOptics -> RTRNSweep -> RRTMLWHeating) and the Dudhia shortwave scheme (DudhiaSW) give rthraten = dthdt_lw + dthdt_sw; the revised MM5 surface layer (SfclayRev) gives u*, z0, Ri_b, wind speed, 10 m wind and the profile functions fm/fh -- YSU's psim/psih arguments are those FULL profile functions, not the stability corrections psim/psih, which are exposed separately; the YSU boundary layer receives them together with rthraten and the land scheme's surface fluxes and returns the tendency vector WRF hands to the dynamics: rthblten, rublten, rvblten, rqvblten, rqcblten, rqiblten, plus rthraten and rth_phys_sum = rthraten + rthblten. Every mounted stage keeps its `input_<x>` rewrite targets for standalone testing; the mount-edge libraries injected here (esm-spec 9.7.10) lower them either to the dumped column state of the step or to the additive `<x>_in` coupling-target parameters that the document's coupling fills from the upstream stage. One document holds one regime; the companion is couplings/scm_physics_column.esm. Regime: WRF step 900 (kernel call 1800), 09:58 UTC = 03:32 local solar time -- the deep stable night of the reference run: gsw = 0 exactly (cos zenith -0.552, so the whole Dudhia branch is the zero-sun path), glw = 251.9, olr = 240.1, slab hfx = -19.08 W/m^2 (SfclayRev's own -19.07), Ri_b = +0.037 (regime 1, stable), u* = 0.267 m/s, a shallow h = 263 m over 6 layers found by the Hong (2010) stable-regime search, tsk = 277.7 K, thin cirrus aloft (qi <= 5.2e-8, four cloudy layers). WHAT IS NOT MOUNTED, and why -- both are EarthSciAST index-set limitations, not physics. (1) The 5-layer SLAB land-surface scheme. Its soil column and the atmospheric column are both the EarthSciDiscretizations grids/column_nonuniform_1d axis `lev`, at 4 and 59 cells; esm index sets are document-scoped and a section 4.7 subsystem-ref edge carries no `prefix`/`rename` (those three fields ride on `expression_template_imports` only, esm-spec 9.7.7 and esm-schema.json $defs/SubsystemRef), so the two sizes cannot coexist under one name. Both components re-export `lev` under the CHILD's metaparameter name NLEV, so mounting slab.esm next to ysu.esm either fails at load with [template_import_index_set_conflict] (whenever the document pins `lev` or the sizes reach the registry in different forms) or, if both mounts are bound to the document's single NLEV, silently forces the 4-layer soil column to the atmosphere's 59 layers -- neither of which is a usable land-surface mount. WRF's order is surface layer -> land surface -> PBL and the PBL receives the LAND scheme's sub-stepped flux, not the surface layer's, so the slab's driver-level hfx/qfx are prescribed here as hfx_lsm/qfx_lsm and coupled into YSU while SfclayRev's own hfx/qfx are exposed and checked separately (the two differ; FORTRAN_BUGS.md N12). couplings/surface_soil_column.esm mounts the slab with the surface layer, which has no atmospheric column and therefore no conflict. (2) The WSM6 MICROPHYSICS. Four of its seven stages (melting_freezing, cold_accretion, ice_deposition, saturation_adjustment) mount hydrometeor_slopes.esm / saturation.esm as section 4.7 subsystems, whose `lev` reaches the document FOLDED to a literal integer, while YSU's `lev` -- which comes from the column_nonuniform_1d grid through an `expression_template_imports` edge -- reaches it SYMBOLICALLY as size \"NLEV\" (the document must therefore declare a metaparameter literally named NLEV and must NOT declare `lev` itself). The two definitions are not deep-equal, so mounting any of those four stages beside YSU fails at load with [template_import_index_set_conflict] models.Pbl EVEN WHEN BOTH SIZES ARE THE SAME INTEGER (verified with a two-mount probe at NLEV = 40 and at 59, with and without threading NLEV into the nested subsystem edge, with the document declaring `lev` symbolically or literally, and with a renamed grid injected at the mount edge). This is the unresolved half of PLAN.md gap (m)/(n): sizing the document's index sets by a literal integer, which is what makes couplings/microphysics_column.esm load, only works when EVERY contributor of that axis arrives folded. Microphysics is in any case a separate driver call at the END of WRF's time step, on the state the RK dynamics leaves behind, so it is not chained to the physics suite even in WRF; the WSM6 chain is couplings/microphysics_column{,_mixed}.esm. KNOWN BINDING LIMITATIONS (Rust CLI, EarthSciAST issue #198): the mounted components' own inline tests are re-run inside this document under the coupling and error, so run `./esm test --model ScmPhysicsColumn couplings/scm_physics_column_night.esm`; the leaves' index sets are redeclared at document level because a top-level ref mount does not merge them; and a parent test cannot set a mounted component's parameter, so the shared surface and radiation scalars are prescribed in this model and coupled in. Residuals of the whole assembly against the step-900 references, measured with zero tolerances: surface-layer outputs <= 2.5e-5 relative -- rmol 2.5e-5, psim 2.4e-5, psih and Ri_b 2.1e-5, hfx 8.5e-6, u* 2.3e-6, qsfc / z0 / regime exact; the stable regime amplifies real32 roundoff in theta_v1 - theta_vs through the bulk Richardson number, an order above the daytime companion -- PBL height 3.5e-6 relative and kpbl exact, K_h / K_m Linf 2.3e-5 m^2/s, longwave fluxes Linf 2.0e-4 (F_up) and 6.2e-4 W/m^2 (F_dn), dthdt_lw and rthraten 5.9e-9 K/s, dthdt_sw and gsw exactly zero, glw 2.6e-7 and olr 1.3e-7 relative, and the PBL tendencies 1.7e-6 K/s (rthblten, column max 7.9e-5), 2.5e-5 and 4.5e-6 m/s^2 (rublten / rvblten, max 5.1e-4 / 2.6e-4), 2.4e-10 1/s (rqvblten, max 1.5e-8), rqcblten exactly zero and rqiblten 2.1e-17 (max 3.1e-15).",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "wrf",
   "eqweather",
   "assembly",
   "coupling",
   "scm",
   "physics-suite",
   "radiation",
   "rrtm",
   "dudhia",
   "surface-layer",
   "pbl",
   "column"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Skamarock, W. C., et al. (2021). A Description of the Advanced Research WRF Model Version 4.3. NCAR Tech. Note NCAR/TN-556+STR."
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 59,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Number of model layers (WRF kte). Bound into the column grid at the import edge; 59 is the em_scm_xy reference column."
  },
  "NBUF": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 44,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Number of buffer layers MM5ATM adds above the model top, nint(p_top / (100 deltap)) with deltap = 4 hPa (RRTMINIT: NLAYERS = kme + nint(p_top*0.01/deltap) - 1); 44 for the reference column (p_top = 177.6 hPa)."
  },
  "NGPT": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 140,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Number of g-points after the 256-to-140 reduction."
  },
  "NBANDS": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 16,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Number of longwave bands."
  },
  "PLANCK_T0": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 159,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. TOTPLNK(i, band) holds the band Planck integral at T = PLANCK_T0 + i kelvin, i = 1..181 (RRTM's INDLEV = INT(T - 159.))."
  },
  "PLANCK_NODES": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 181,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Temperature nodes of the TOTPLNK table (160..340 K)."
  }
 },
