   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "scm_step900_physics_column",
     "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, p_top = 177.6 hPa, data/eqwefic/scm_ref) dumped by the instrumented ctessum-claude/WRF fork (module_esm_dump, commit 592f693) at TWO levels for the same step: the PHYSICS-DRIVER level (hooks around radiation_driver, surface_driver + pbl_driver and the physics-tendency sum in dyn_em/module_first_rk_step_part1.F -- dumps subassembly_all, _pbl and _rad) and the KERNEL level (sfclayrev, sw, ysu and rrtm scm_ref dumps of the same call). The seven dumps are merged into one column namespace by tools/merge_dumps.py (esm_dump_scm_suite_<step>.json, variables tagged all_/pbl_/rad_/sfc_/sw_/ysu_/rrtm_) because tools/fill_tests.py admits two dumps per test; the numbers are transcribed by fill_tests.py from the sidecar couplings/scm_physics_column_night.esm.fill.json. All references are real32 model values. The DRIVER-level tendency vector (rthblten, rublten, rvblten, rqvblten, rqcblten, rqiblten, rthraten, rth_phys_sum, hfx, qfx, gsw, glw, olr, pblh) is the contract this document exists to pin: it is what WRF hands to the dynamics, and rqcblten/rqiblten are asserted here for the first time. Regime: WRF step 900 (kernel call 1800), 09:58 UTC = 03:32 local solar time -- the deep stable night of the reference run: gsw = 0 exactly (cos zenith -0.552, so the whole Dudhia branch is the zero-sun path), glw = 251.9, olr = 240.1, slab hfx = -19.08 W/m^2 (SfclayRev's own -19.07), Ri_b = +0.037 (regime 1, stable), u* = 0.267 m/s, a shallow h = 263 m over 6 layers found by the Hong (2010) stable-regime search, tsk = 277.7 K, thin cirrus aloft (qi <= 5.2e-8, four cloudy layers). Residuals of the whole assembly against the step-900 references, measured with zero tolerances: surface-layer outputs <= 2.5e-5 relative -- rmol 2.5e-5, psim 2.4e-5, psih and Ri_b 2.1e-5, hfx 8.5e-6, u* 2.3e-6, qsfc / z0 / regime exact; the stable regime amplifies real32 roundoff in theta_v1 - theta_vs through the bulk Richardson number, an order above the daytime companion -- PBL height 3.5e-6 relative and kpbl exact, K_h / K_m Linf 2.3e-5 m^2/s, longwave fluxes Linf 2.0e-4 (F_up) and 6.2e-4 W/m^2 (F_dn), dthdt_lw and rthraten 5.9e-9 K/s, dthdt_sw and gsw exactly zero, glw 2.6e-7 and olr 1.3e-7 relative, and the PBL tendencies 1.7e-6 K/s (rthblten, column max 7.9e-5), 2.5e-5 and 4.5e-6 m/s^2 (rublten / rvblten, max 5.1e-4 / 2.6e-4), 2.4e-10 1/s (rqvblten, max 1.5e-8), rqcblten exactly zero and rqiblten 2.1e-17 (max 3.1e-15). The PBL TENDENCIES are asserted only LOOSELY and document a known gap rather than test the physics: WRF's rthblten/rublten/rvblten/rqvblten/rqcblten/rqiblten are the IMPLICIT tridiagonal step's (c_new - c_old)/dt at dt = 60 s while the assembly evaluates the instantaneous right-hand side (PLAN.md 0.3), which at this regime is the dominant term of their residual; the physics itself is pinned by ysu.esm's own small-dt tests, and a stage-3 comparison at the WRF step must apply the same implicit step to the assembled tendencies. The driver-level th2/t2/q2 are overwritten by the land-surface branch of surface_driver, so those three are referenced to the kernel-level sfclayrev dump, and the slab's driver-level hfx/qfx are prescribed (hfx_lsm/qfx_lsm) because the land scheme is not co-mounted -- see the model description. TOLERANCES: each is the smallest of {1, 2, 5} x 10^k that is at least 5x the residual measured in a zero-tolerance run (relative for the scalars, absolute for the Linf_error column assertions), with a 1e-6 relative floor; an assertion that is exact at zero tolerance keeps abs 0. ",
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "psfc0": 97135.1484375,
      "tsk0": 277.69512939453125,
      "xland0": 1.0,
      "mavail0": 0.6000000238418579,
      "pblh_prev0": 262.73492431640625,
      "u10": 3.8598763942718506,
      "v10": -3.4375851154327393,
      "t10": 278.6571044921875,
      "qv10": 0.00493006594479084,
      "p10": 96836.0546875,
      "dz10": 50.50978088378906,
      "dx0": 4000.0,
      "lakemask0": 0.0,
      "water_depth0": 0.0,
      "znt_prev0": 0.05000000074505806,
      "ust_prev0": 0.2666873335838318,
      "mol_prev0": 0.058637551963329315,
      "qsfc_prev0": 0.005456671584397554,
      "hfx_prev0": -19.10153579711914,
      "qfx_prev0": 2.971125013573328e-06,
      "ustm_prev0": 0.2666873335838318,
      "chs_prev0": 0.0,
      "chs2_prev0": 0.0,
      "cqs2_prev0": 0.6562437415122986,
      "isfflx0": 1.0,
      "shalwater_z00": 0.0,
      "scm_force_flux0": 0.0,
      "isftcflx0": 0.0,
      "iz0tlnd0": 0.0,
      "topdown0": 1.0,
      "hfx_lsm0": -19.078828811645508,
      "qfx_lsm0": 2.9627963158418424e-06,
      "co2vmr0": 0.00037900000461377203,
      "n2ovmr0": 3.1900000863060995e-07,
      "ch4vmr0": 1.7739999975674436e-06,
      "emiss0": 0.9200000166893005,
      "csza0": -0.5521889328956604,
      "albedo0": 0.20000000298023224,
      "solcon0": 1384.8056640625,
      "obscur0": 0.0,
      "cssca0": 9.999999747378752e-06,
      "icloud0": 1.0
     },
     "time_span": {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 1
     },
     "assertions": [
      {
       "variable": "sfc_hfx",
       "time": 0.0,
       "expected": -19.073570251464844,
       "tolerance": {
        "rel": 5e-05
       }
      },
      {
